# Optional build-time PUBLIC configuration. Leave all three empty for the local prototype.
# Configure all three together only after owner RLS and deployment protection are verified.
# Never supply a Supabase secret/service-role key, provider token or database password.
ORBIT_SUPABASE_URL=
ORBIT_SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=
ORBIT_SITE_URL=
# URL: HTTPS outside localhost/127.0.0.1/[::1]; Supabase URL must be an origin.
# Key: sb_publishable_... or legacy anon-role JWT for disposable local Supabase.
# Site URL: exact authorized application redirect on this origin, without query/fragment.
# Preview-only fallback: if unset, VERCEL_ENV=preview plus a safe VERCEL_URL *.vercel.app
# supplies the immutable preview origin. Production/local cloud builds require ORBIT_SITE_URL.
# Builds emit only these public fields plus publicRelease:false. Public release is disabled.
# No dotenv loader: use your shell/CI/Vercel environment; this example is never served.
# Production cannot fall back to local mode. It also requires the reviewed public
# origins in release/production-target.json and an exact matching private CSP.
# Preview-scoped variables are not evidence of Production-scoped configuration.
